Reading a fence escapes every non-ASCII character.

`title: Café` comes back as `title: "Caf\xE9"`.

Frontmatter.serializeYAML calls Yams.dump without setting allowUnicode,
and that parameter defaults to false, which tells libyaml to escape
every character outside ASCII. The value survives a round trip, but the
text a person reads does not: an accent, a dash, an emoji or any CJK
text turns into hex escapes.

It is worse than an ugly read. `--set -i` writes the same bytes back,
so setting one key rewrites every non-ASCII value in the file as escape
sequences.

Yams.dump should be called with allowUnicode: true.
